qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   April 3, 2024|pn|hondo717,Honeydog3,ladydoc,aspiring|
md|2SJT76HJ83DKT4CT83,SAKQ4HQ62DAJ862C5,S9HAK54DQ3CAQ9742,S8532HT97D975CKJ6|sv|b|
mb|1D|mb|2C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|2@C is one of my favorite bids over 1@D. It is kind of preemptive and makes it much harder for the opponents to find a major suit fit. I recommend you strain to bid 2@C over 1@D whenever you can.|
PG| ***** 65 ***** |


mb|P?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I would like to bid 3@C but I am too weak plus 4-3-3-3 distribution is terrible.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


mb|P|mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|For two reasons West should make a double here. One is partner might have hearts and two, partner might have a penalty pass. By that I mean since a double of 2@C is negative East is unable to make a penalty double and will sometimes (although admittedly somewhat rarely) want to make a penalty double.|
PG| ***** 67 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So whenever you open and there is an overcall and it goes pass pass you should at least think about the possibility that partner has a penalty double particularly if you are short in the opponent's suit.|
PG| ***** 68 ***** |


mb|D|mb|R|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|2D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The redouble by North shows a good hand so I am going to bid 3@C.|
PG| ***** 69 ***** |


mb|3C|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Normally I would not bid 3@D with the West hand. Admittedly it is not clear how many diamonds your side has but if partner has 4 diamonds he probably has a weak hand because he might very well bid 2@D over 2@C with 4 diamonds. |
PG| ***** 70 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So likely he has 3 meaning they have an 8 card fit and |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| dictates a pass. |
PG| ***** 71 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Further, I have some additional rules for bidding ^*B3 over 3^*n. First of course, you should do so with a 9-card fit as the Law dictates. Second do it if you have a singleton, particularly in the opponents suit. That is why I agree with West bidding 3@D--singleton club.|
PG| ***** 72 ***** |


